`make validate` now passes all schema, Python, and Go checks. The literal `make regenerate-check` target compares generated files to the real Git index, so it correctly reports the intentional new v6 files as a diff in an uncommitted producer worktree. I’m validating it against a task-local alternate index snapshot of the intended generated baseline—without touching the repository’s real staging area—and also comparing two full conformance tree digests.
